---
const problems = [
    {
        num: "01",
        title: "Progress leaks",
        body: "Learn WebSockets tonight, rebuild the context next week. Nothing compounds.",
    },
    {
        num: "02",
        title: "The hour disappears",
        body: "Docs to search to another tab. The free hour is gone before you write a line.",
    },
    {
        num: "03",
        title: "Weekends reset you",
        body: "Cram on Saturday, start from zero on Monday. Consistency beats binge sessions.",
    },
];
---

<section class="problem">
    <div class="problem-panel">
        <header class="problem-head">
            <h2 class="problem-title">
                You're not short on tutorials.<br />
                You're short on time, and nothing sticks.
            </h2>
            <p class="problem-sub">
                Watching, prompting, and skimming docs is easy. Owning a skill
                after a full day of work is hard.<br />
                Learnist exists for that gap.
            </p>
        </header>

        <ul class="problem-grid">
            {
                problems.map((item) => (
                    <li class="problem-card">
                        <span class="problem-num">{item.num}</span>
                        <h3 class="problem-card-title">{item.title}</h3>
                        <p class="problem-card-body">{item.body}</p>
                    </li>
                ))
            }
        </ul>

        <figure class="note">
            <blockquote class="note-quote">
                <p class="note-lead">
                    I built Learnist for myself. New city, offline job, maybe an
                    hour a day. I didn't want courses, I didn't want to raw-dog
                    docs for hours, and I definitely didn't want to copy-paste
                    code I couldn't explain.
                </p>
                <p class="note-body">
                    A week in, something changed. Walking to work, Learnist was
                    in my ear: what I got right, what I got wrong, the next
                    challenge. Finish it, get the hit, want the next one. I was
                    doing lessons at 6am because I wanted to.
                </p>
            </blockquote>
            <figcaption class="note-by">
                Ram, engineer &amp; creator of Learnist
            </figcaption>
        </figure>
    </div>
</section>

<style>
    .problem {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 2;
        padding: 0 0 4rem;
        color: var(--ink);
    }

    .problem-panel {
        overflow: hidden;
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        padding: 3.5rem 2rem 3.75rem;

        /*
         * Artwork is blue at the rim and near-white at the core, but the core
         * is a fixed slice of the image and the content is taller than it.
         * This wash extends that white centre so dark text stays readable
         * while the blue rim survives.
         */
        --wash: radial-gradient(
            ellipse 64% 60% at 50% 50%,
            rgb(255 255 255 / 0.97) 0%,
            rgb(255 255 255 / 0.94) 46%,
            rgb(255 255 255 / 0.72) 66%,
            rgb(255 255 255 / 0) 80%
        );

        background:
            var(--wash),
            url("/second_section_background.png") center / cover no-repeat,
            #2563eb;
    }

    .problem-head {
        max-width: 38rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .problem-title {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.8vw, 2rem);
        line-height: 1.18;
        letter-spacing: -0.03em;
        font-weight: 700;
        text-wrap: balance;
    }

    .problem-sub {
        margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        line-height: 1.55;
        color: var(--muted);
        text-wrap: pretty;
    }

    /* ---------- Numbered cards ---------- */

    .problem-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
        margin: 2.25rem 0 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.55);
        box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgb(20 17 15 / 0.04);
    }

    .problem-card {
        padding: 1.35rem 1.4rem 1.5rem;
    }

    /* Hairline rules between columns, as in the reference. */
    .problem-card + .problem-card {
        border-left: 1px solid rgb(20 17 15 / 0.09);
    }

    .problem-num {
        display: block;
        font-size: 0.7rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: 0.02em;
        color: var(--accent);
    }

    .problem-card-title {
        margin: 0.85rem 0 0.4rem;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        font-weight: 650;
        letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    }

    .problem-card-body {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        line-height: 1.5;
        color: var(--muted);
        text-wrap: pretty;
    }

    /* ---------- Founder note ---------- */

    .note {
        margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
        padding: 1.6rem 1.85rem 1.75rem;
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.72);
        box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgb(20 17 15 / 0.04);
    }

    .note-quote {
        margin: 0;
        max-width: 48rem;
    }

    .note-lead {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 1.4vw, 1.1rem);
        line-height: 1.45;
        letter-spacing: -0.015em;
        font-weight: 600;
        text-wrap: pretty;
    }

    .note-body {
        margin: 0.85rem 0 0;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        line-height: 1.55;
        color: var(--muted);
        max-width: 42rem;
        text-wrap: pretty;
    }

    .note-by {
        margin: 1.1rem 0 0;
        font-size: 0.82rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--accent);
    }

    @media (max-width: 860px) {
        .problem {
            padding-bottom: 3rem;
        }

        .problem-panel {
            padding: 2.75rem 1.15rem 3rem;
            --wash: radial-gradient(
                ellipse 92% 62% at 50% 50%,
                rgb(255 255 255 / 0.97) 0%,
                rgb(255 255 255 / 0.94) 55%,
                rgb(255 255 255 / 0.75) 74%,
                rgb(255 255 255 / 0) 92%
            );
        }

        .problem-grid {
            grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
        }

        .problem-card + .problem-card {
            border-left: 0;
            border-top: 1px solid rgb(20 17 15 / 0.09);
        }

        .note {
            padding: 1.35rem 1.25rem 1.5rem;
        }
    }
</style>
